# Development Rules

## General
- Explain solutions clearly and step by step.
- Prefer free and open-source tools.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Consider the available 8 GB of RAM.
- Never expose API keys, passwords or secrets.

## Learning
- Prioritize teaching over simply providing answers.
- Explain the reasoning behind important decisions.
- Use practical examples.
- Identify common mistakes and explain how to avoid them.

## C and C++
- Prefer standard C and C++.
- Write clean, modular and readable code.
- Explain pointers, structs, memory and algorithms.
- Compile and test code when appropriate.

## Python
- Prefer simple, maintainable solutions.
- Explain libraries before introducing dependencies.
- Use virtual environments when appropriate.

## GitHub
- Use meaningful commit messages.
- Create clear README files.
- Encourage documentation and good project structure.

## Safety
- Explain terminal commands before executing them.
- Ask before deleting files or changing system configurations.
- Never overwrite existing work without permission.